## Project Overview\
This project is a simple Mood Tracker web app hosted on GitHub Pages.\
\
The app should allow users to:\
- Select their mood each day using emoji/icons\
- Add optional notes\
- View mood history\
- View a simple chart of moods over time\
- Save all data locally in the browser using localStorage\
- Work fully offline after loading\
- Be mobile-friendly and simple to use\
\
The project should use:\
- HTML\
- CSS\
- JavaScript (no backend)\
- localStorage for saving data\
- GitHub Pages for hosting\
\
Do NOT use:\
- Databases\
- Servers\
- Authentication systems\
- Complex frameworks unless absolutely necessary\
\
Keep the project beginner-friendly and easy to understand.\
\
---\
\
# App Requirements\
\
## Main Features\
\
### 1. Mood Entry\
Users can:\
- Choose a mood from emoji buttons:\
  - \uc0\u55357 \u56832  Happy\
  - \uc0\u55357 \u56848  Neutral\
  - \uc0\u55357 \u56866  Sad\
  - \uc0\u55357 \u56865  Angry\
  - \uc0\u55357 \u56884  Tired\
  - \uc0\u55357 \u56845  Excited\
- Add a short note\
- Save the entry\
\
Each entry should automatically include:\
- Current date\
- Current time\
\
---\
\
### 2. Mood History\
Display previous mood entries in:\
- A clean list\
- Most recent first\
\
Each item should show:\
- Mood emoji\
- Mood name\
- Note\
- Date/time\
\
Allow users to:\
- Delete entries\
- Clear all entries with confirmation\
\
---\
\
### 3. Mood Chart\
Create a simple chart showing mood trends over time.\
\
Suggested tools:\
- Chart.js preferred\
\
The chart should:\
- Update automatically\
- Read from saved localStorage data\
\
